Z||000000||falconhulk||11-06-2001||08:07 AM||||Well I happen to be thumbing through a chey high perf this morning and came upon an article about the new Vortec 4200 inline 6.  it seems this realitively light wieght motor pumps out 270hp.  It was originally designed for trucks so the TQ is on the low end!  Seems these motors are a perfect place to start for a hot rod.  The ignition system has no moving parts and no plug wires to go bad!  It will even continue to run if one of the crank or cam positon sensors goes bad and just pop on the check engine light.  Now....anyone know if this would be a good fit in a fiero?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Hank is Here||11-06-2001||09:32 AM||||I have tought about this and basically it is an I6 engine, I doubt that it would fit, heck it is probably longer than a V8.  No fact at all just my thoughts||||reg||1
